y−1 and of row y+1 have the same colour.\n- Those two cells sit at the same x.\n- Row y is background at that x.\n\nI have not run this check. When I reason through the six rows the verifier flagged, each of them breaks the same‑x requirement. The rows released in pairs 1 and 3 (for example pair 1 row 11) satisfy it. The corridor walk itself is unchanged.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid).copy()\n    H, W = g.shape\n    bg = background(g)\n    marker = g[0, 0]\n    out = g.copy()\n\n    def first_cell(r):\n        for x in range(1, W):\n            if g[r, x] != bg:\n                return x, g[r, x]\n        return None, None\n\n    def corridor_ok(r, c, d):\n        if not (0 <= r < H and 0 <= c < W) or g[r, c] != bg:\n            return False\n        dy, dx = d\n        a = (r + dx, c + dy)\n        b = (r - dx, c - dy)\n        for (yy, xx) in (a, b):\n            if not (0 <= yy < H and 0 <= xx < W):\n                return False\n        va, vb = g[a], g[b]\n        return va != bg and vb != bg and va == vb\n\n    for y in range(1, H - 1):\n        if g[y, 0] != marker or g[y, 1] != bg:\n            continue\n        xa, ca = first_cell(y - 1)\n        xb, cb = first_cell(y + 1)\n        if ca is None or cb is None or ca != cb or xa != xb or g[y, xa] != bg:\n            continue\n        r, c = y, 1\n        d = (0, 1)\n        steps = 0\n        while steps < 4 * H * W:\n            steps += 1\n            nr, nc = r + d[0], c + d[1]\n            if 0 <= nr < H and 0 <= nc < W and g[nr, nc] == bg:\n                r, c = nr, nc\n                continue\n            opts = []\n            for nd in ((d[1], d[0]), (-d[1], -d[0])):\n                if corridor_ok(r + nd[0], c + nd[1], nd):\n                    opts.append(nd)\n            if len(opts) == 1:\n                d = opts[0]\n                r, c = r + d[0], c + d[1]\n                continue\n            break\n        out[y, 0] = bg\n        out[r, c] = marker\n        emit(out.copy(), f\"Row {y} is a gap between two bars of colour {ca} starting at x={xa}: its {marker} \"\n                         f\"leaves the stripe, walks the corridor and is placed at its dead end ({r},{c}).\")\n\n    emit(out.copy(), \"All corridor markers relocated; final grid.\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"paths":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"The corridor walk itself is unchanged."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Row 1 is a gap between two bars of colour 1 starting at x=2: its 6 leaves the stripe, walks the corridor and is placed at its dead end (1,15)."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Row 5 is a gap between two bars of colour 4 starting at x=2: its 6 leaves the stripe, walks the corridor and is placed at its dead end (0,14)."}],"analogy":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"The rows released in pairs 1 and 3 (for example pair 1 row 11) satisfy it."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"6538f5a405c4b400aae391c8cd6a95816ffcfbcc6e0854e9fcca7553fd7dd8b4","task_sha256":"abf585f038055cc3dae8043bc98977154f52137ec417b81e889a2a1c5e118003","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
